<BaseLayout title="About the Author" description="About Randy Brown, the author of Rhythm Rascal drum machine software.">
  <h3>About the Author</h3>
  <p>
    <img class="floatRight" src="/images/riz-2004.jpg" width="300" alt="Randy Brown" />
  </p>
  <p>
    Rhythm Rascal was designed and written by me, Randy Brown.&nbsp; It is my hobby project.&nbsp; I also develop
    software professionally full time.&nbsp; I write software systems for
    <a href="https://www.agilairecorp.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">air quality monitoring</a>.&nbsp; I have been
    working on Rhythm Rascal since 2003, after being dissatisfied with the features of most drum sequencer applications,
    particularly in regard to heavy metal music.&nbsp; My goal with this product is to provide a powerful, but
    easy-to-use drum machine for guitarists writing and performing complex music styles.
  </p>
  <p>
    I live in Corryton, TN, just outside of Knoxville, with my wife and two children.&nbsp; I have played guitar and
    other instruments in several local bands in the past.
  </p>
  <h3><a href="/contact/">Contact me</a> for more details about Rhythm Rascal</h3>
</BaseLayout>
